# OIS / workspace wiring

## Precedence (drift disputes)

1. Local `git` for the four OIS roots (see `docs/INTEGRITY_SYNC_BATCH_ALGORITHM.md` Part 2.1).
2. Monorepo submodule gitlink: `git ls-tree HEAD Projects/GRID-main` inside `CascadeProjects` when that checkout exists.
3. OIS Part 2.1 checkpoint table (dated rows).
4. Orbit memo / external dashboards last — never treat seeds-only scores as proof of submodule alignment.

## Rituals

- Run `make orbit-snapshot` (or `bash scripts/oissnapshot.sh`) after material git events or before claiming ecosystem sync. Prefer env **`CASCADE_WORKSPACE_ROOT`** for the monorepo checkout path (see `scripts/oissnapshot.sh`).
- Run `make audit` locally for the same path as CI; `make audit-strict` for full OSV without interim CVE ignore (expect possible non-zero exit).

## Rhyme-and-reasons / Semantic Officer

- Do not invent or cite runtime symbols from `combined_space.py` / `control_room/*` unless those files are present in the active workspace and were read in this session. Prose checkpoints are fine; code-backed symbol audits are out-of-zoom unless the operator expands scope.
